Feature: Heikin-Ashi Reversal Confirmed by RSI
  Primary timeframe: 1h
  Parameter reversal_streak default 3
  Parameter oversold default 30
  Parameter overbought default 70
  Parameter stop_loss_pct default 2
  Parameter take_profit_pct default 4

  # The most-cited Heikin-Ashi pairing: an HA colour-change reversal is acted on
  # only when RSI confirms an exhausted move. Two exit paths per side demonstrate
  # OR-logic (duplicate scenarios sharing the same Then). HA alone lags, so the
  # RSI confirmation is what keeps the entries honest.

  Scenario: Enter long on a bullish HA reversal from oversold
    Given no open position
    When ha_bullish_reversal(reversal_streak)
    And rsi_oversold(oversold)
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 + take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit long when RSI reaches overbought
    Given a long position is open
    When rsi_overbought(overbought)
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Exit long on a strong bearish HA candle
    Given a long position is open
    When ha_strong_bearish()
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short on a bearish HA reversal from overbought
    Given no open position
    When ha_bearish_reversal(reversal_streak)
    And rsi_overbought(overbought)
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 - take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit short when RSI reaches oversold
    Given a short position is open
    When rsi_oversold(oversold)
    Then short_exit

  Scenario: Exit short on a strong bullish HA candle
    Given a short position is open
    When ha_strong_bullish()
    Then short_exit
